<h1>Dongle</h1>
<div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;" align="center">
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3"></div>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> The dongle is a hardware key (also known as hardware lock or activation key) which activates the software. The dongle also controls which software features are enabled, using a password system. Passwords are 48 digit hexadecimal numbers. A password is supplied with the system when it is installed.</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">A dongle can be re-programmed any time for additional options. There are two numbers required for enabling the dongle for new options:</span></p>
